winewayland: gate the SC_MOVE decline -- it caused the half-white splash

Patch zzp (11.10-64) had two halves: the caption widening, which was gated, and
the SC_MOVE decline, which was NOT. Turning the feature off therefore did not
restore the old behaviour, and the ungated half went out to every user.

Bisected with a screenshot harness that measures white coverage of the splash
area during startup (the fault lasts about one frame in fourteen, which is why
eyeballing missed it):

    11.10-63   0.0% white   clean
    11.10-64  73.6% white   broken
    11.10-65  72.9% white   broken, with every subsurface gate OFF

64's only engine change over 63 is zzp, and the gated half was off in the 65
run, so the ungated SC_MOVE decline is what is left. Also ruled out by
measurement, not assumption: the seed-skip path from the previous splash bug
(TODO.md P1o) is NOT involved -- 72.9% with it on and 72.9% with it off.

Now behind NEUTRON_SYSCOMMAND_DECLINE, default OFF, which is 11.10-63's
behaviour exactly. It stays available because a captioned subsurface cannot be
dragged without it, and that is needed for the docked-or-floating panel work.

RULE, restated because it just cost a release: every behaviour change in this
driver gets its own gate. An ungated change cannot be A/B'd, cannot be reverted
by a tester, and hides inside the feature it shipped with.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -377,6 +377,23 @@
  * dialog class; 1302 did not and none was. The extension panel this whole line of work exists for
  * does NOT carry it, so excluding them costs the feature nothing. Exposed as its own gate purely
  * so the effect can be isolated on a tester's machine. */
+/* NEUTRON: decline SC_MOVE/SC_SIZE when we did NOT hand the interaction to the compositor,
+ * so win32u runs its own move loop. Added ungated in 11.10-64 to make a captioned subsurface
+ * draggable -- and 11.10-64 is exactly where the Premiere splash started rendering its left half
+ * white. Bisected 2026-08-27 with a screenshot harness: 63 = 0.0% white, 64 = 73.6%, 65 = 72.9%
+ * with every subsurface gate OFF, and 64's only engine change over 63 is this patch. The caption
+ * half is gated and off, so this ungated half is what is left.
+ *
+ * ⛔ Every behaviour change in this driver must be gated. This one was not, which is why turning
+ * off the feature it belongs to did not restore the old behaviour. Default OFF = 11.10-63's
+ * behaviour exactly. */
+static BOOL neutron_syscommand_decline(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_SYSCOMMAND_DECLINE"); on = (e && e[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0; }
+    return on;
+}
+
 static BOOL neutron_owned_subsurface_modal(void)
 {
     static int on = -1;
@@ -1636,6 +1653,8 @@
                 /* NEUTRON: claim it only when the COMPOSITOR now owns the interaction. */
                 ret = 0;
             }
+            /* gated: without the gate this restores 11.10-63's unconditional claim */
+            if (!neutron_syscommand_decline()) ret = 0;
             pthread_mutex_unlock(&process_wayland.seat.mutex);
             wayland_win_data_release(data);
             /* NEUTRON: ret stays -1 when we did NOT hand the move/resize to the compositor.
